=== cold-open: the harness, driven by a stub reader ===
  PASS  --brief prints the front-door fingerprint the gate will demand
  PASS  --brief prints the SHIPPED prompt verbatim — a cold open with an improvised question is not reproducible
  PASS  --brief files nothing — printing the question is not answering it
  PASS  --run with an arbitrary reader-cmd files a transcript — the reader is a SEAM, not a vendor
  PASS  the reader runs IN the repository — it has to be looking at the thing it is describing
  PASS  the reader gets the verbatim prompt on stdin
  PASS  ...with the repository path substituted, so the reader knows what to look at
  PASS  a second reading of the same front door on the same day is filed BESIDE the first, never over it
  PASS  the transcript carries **Surface-fingerprint:**
  PASS  the transcript carries **Prompt-fingerprint:**
  PASS  the transcript carries **Reader:**
  PASS  the transcript carries **Run-by:**
  PASS  the transcript carries **Date:**
  PASS  the transcript stamps the PROMPT's hash — change a question and every transcript stops counting, because nobody has answered the new one
  PASS  the reader's own words are in the transcript — the transcript IS the product
  PASS  the checked-claims table records that the reader came away with the entry point
  PASS  a reader who MISSED the entry point is recorded as a 'no' and the transcript is still filed — the finding is the product, not a failure
  PASS  a reader that FAILS files nothing — an empty transcript would satisfy the gate while proving nobody read anything
  PASS  a reader that says NOTHING files nothing
  PASS  reading a STALE page is refused — a transcript about a document nobody has seen is a fresh-looking lie
  PASS  --check exits 1 when no reader has seen the current front door
  PASS  --check exits 0 once a current transcript is on file
  PASS  --check goes red again the moment the front door changes
  PASS  --record files a HUMAN reading with the same stamps — the offline path is a first-class path, not a bypass
  PASS  --record without --reader is refused — the one thing the machine cannot check is the one thing it must at least record
  PASS  a missing prompt file is a LOUD refusal — without a fixed question there is no reproducible exercise
  PASS  the default reader runs with --safe-mode: no CLAUDE.md, no plugins, no hooks, no skills, no memory — a reader that loaded this project's own doctrine would not be cold
  PASS  the default reader is READ-ONLY — it is here to report what it found, not to fix it
  PASS  cold-open.sh and ceo-todos-render.sh are executable
  PASS  ONBOARDING-RUNBOOK.md names ceo-todos-init.sh — an adopter is told the CEO's TODOs exist
  PASS  skills/bootstrap-interview/SKILL.md names ceo-todos-init.sh — an adopter is told the CEO's TODOs exist

